# i386 configuration for libassistant.
# LplAssistant compiled -ffreestanding into libassistant.a, exactly as libengine
# does for LplPlugin. Server profile only: a headless image renders nothing, so the
# budget a client spends on rasterising is spent here on inference instead.
#
# As with libengine, the source list is EXPLICIT and must be kept in lock-step with
# the xmake build. A glob would silently pull a hosted backend into ring 0.
#
# Determinism flags identical to libengine: -msse2 -mfpmath=sse -ffp-contract=off
# -fno-math-errno -mstackrealign. Anything linked into the kernel obeys one
# arithmetic contract, not one per library.
ARCH_CXXFLAGS=-msse2 -mfpmath=sse -ffp-contract=off -fno-math-errno -mstackrealign
ARCH_CPPFLAGS=

# LplAssistant sources compiled into libassistant.a (paths relative to
# LPLASSISTANT_ROOT).
#
# infer/ and mind/. voice/, research/ and backend/ stay out: they are hosted by
# contract — they parse text, speak HTTP and allocate freely, which is the writer half
# of the reader/writer line the whole project is drawn along.
#
# mind/ appears as NINE files rather than as the module: Conversation.cpp is the one
# turn that talks to a real model over a real vector store, so it holds std::string and
# links libpq. It lives in its own hosted target next door for that reason, and this
# list is where that boundary is actually enforced.
#
# infer/src/Types.cpp is deliberately absent. Its header carries ChatMessage, which
# holds a std::string because it crosses into prompt templates verbatim — a hosted
# type, in a file whose other consumers are hosted. Nothing on this side includes it.
#
# Nothing here calls libm. The exponential a softmax needs comes from
# math::fixedExp2, the square root a normalisation needs from math::fixedSqrt, and
# the rotary angles from CORDIC — which is the whole reason the rotary frequency
# ladder is base two rather than the usual base ten thousand.
# satellite/ is here too, and for a reason worth stating: it is the ONLY module in
# the project with three consumers that share no instruction set — a hosted node, this
# kernel, and an eventual microcontroller firmware. Three implementations of a wire
# format is three chances to disagree about what closes an utterance.
ARCH_ASSISTANT_SRCS=\
satellite/src/Protocol.cpp \
satellite/src/VoiceActivity.cpp \
satellite/src/WakeWord.cpp \
satellite/src/Duplex.cpp \
satellite/src/PowerState.cpp \
satellite/src/Parity.cpp \
infer/src/Quant.cpp \
infer/src/Tensor.cpp \
infer/src/TensorArena.cpp \
infer/src/Vocab.cpp \
infer/src/Tokenizer.cpp \
infer/src/Model.cpp \
infer/src/KvCache.cpp \
infer/src/Attention.cpp \
infer/src/FeedForward.cpp \
infer/src/Transformer.cpp \
infer/src/Sampler.cpp \
infer/src/GrammarSampler.cpp \
infer/src/Inference.cpp \
infer/src/Parity.cpp \
mind/src/Persona.cpp \
mind/src/Intent.cpp \
mind/src/Budget.cpp \
mind/src/Memory.cpp \
mind/src/Recall.cpp \
mind/src/ReAct.cpp \
mind/src/Reasoning.cpp \
mind/src/Dialogue.cpp \
mind/src/Parity.cpp \
